likelier: working from home or a rented room; no colleagues nearby; a first submission to a demanding journal or funder
rarer: a shared workspace or a host lab; a submission that was accepted
scene: The rejection comes on a Thursday: three short reviews, one of them unkind. With no group around, there is nobody in the corridor to say it happens to everyone. The room is very quiet.
scene W: {N} reads the reviews the way a judge reads a case: which points are fair, which are not, and what the rules allow in reply.
scene U: Under the unkind tone, one reviewer has found a real gap in the analysis. {N} hates to admit it, and cannot stop thinking about it.
scene B: The unkind reviewer writes a lot like {rival}. {N} files that away for later.
scene R: {N} wants to fire off a reply tonight, every word of it true and burning.
scene G: In the old days {mentor} would have been down the hall. {N} looks at the phone for a long time.
- W | answer every point in order, concede the fair ones, and send it out again | v: conformity, achievement | chance: 85
- U | rerun the analysis to close the gap the harsh reviewer found | v: achievement, universalism | self_control: + | grants: statistical judgment | chance: 72
- B | send it unchanged to the next journal on the list the same afternoon | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 60
- R | write the reviewers a furious reply tonight, and send it | v: self-direction | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: an angry letter to anonymous reviewers; backfire: the editor remembers the name | self_control: - | chance: 35
- G | let it sit for a week, and walk every day before reading it again | v: tradition, security | self_control: + | chance: 75
- W>B | ask the editor, through the proper channel, whether a revised version would be considered | v: achievement, power | chance: 40
- U>R | turn the harsh review into a sharper, bolder second version | v: self-direction, stimulation | chance: 70
- B>G | take the steady post you were offered, and let the fellowship go | v: security | drops: independent investigator | self_control: - | chance: 92
- R>W | ring a friend who was rejected too, and agree to swap drafts every month | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 88
- G>U | ring your old supervisor and ask which criticisms are worth answering | door | v: tradition, achievement | chance: 80
works: Within the week {N} is back at the work, and the next version is stronger for the beating.
works: The silence breaks: someone {N} trusts reads the paper and says plainly what it needs.
fails: The paper sits in a folder for a month while {N} avoids it.
fails: The second journal says no as well, and {N} starts to wonder who the work is for.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 62. step 2, transform (cycle s3)

== whose question is this, really
tier: inner
threshold: title:independent investigator
step: 2
transform: yes
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 25-95
times: once, in the first months after becoming an independent investigator, for the perhaps 1 in 2 whose question has already drifted from the proposal; across all lives about 1 in 4,000 (estimate)
holds: independent investigator
stakes: .8
tone: mixed
life: work, meaning
horizon: years
